00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:37.040
Digitimes reports that TSMC's acquisition of an AUO plant is reshaping the panel supply

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:37.380
chain.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:43.757
A two-phase cold plate takes heat off a processor by boiling liquid at the chip, then carries

00:06:43.757 --> 00:06:47.217
vapor to a condenser that dumps the heat and sends liquid back.

00:06:47.717 --> 00:06:50.177
Sensible cooling has to warm a stream of fluid.

00:06:50.817 --> 00:06:56.017
Boiling spends that energy as latent heat, so less fluid moves more load, and the plate

00:06:56.017 --> 00:06:59.117
can sit on the package instead of asking the room air to do it.

00:06:59.617 --> 00:07:01.097
The condenser is still required.

00:07:01.617 --> 00:07:06.437
Heat is not gone until the far side of the loop rejects it, and in a rack that far side

00:07:06.437 --> 00:07:11.237
is a coolant distribution unit tied into whatever water or air the building already runs.

00:07:11.977 --> 00:07:15.817
HPC wires right up of Excelsius puts that loop in one frame.

00:07:16.297 --> 00:07:21.397
The new cool IR-150, a fully integrated IT rack plus CDU.

00:07:22.017 --> 00:07:27.037
Excelsius calls it the first of that kind and is handing it to Villanova as shared infrastructure,

00:07:27.517 --> 00:07:28.677
not as a bench demo.

00:07:29.237 --> 00:07:31.817
The company is in the NVIDIA Inception program.

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:37.297
The recipient is the National Science Foundation Center for Energy Smart Electronic Systems.

00:07:37.817 --> 00:07:40.797
Villanova is one of three university sites in that center.

00:07:41.457 --> 00:07:46.357
Excelsius already backs a separate cooler chips project at the University of Texas at Arlington,

00:07:46.997 --> 00:07:48.357
under Derek J. Agonefer.

00:07:49.177 --> 00:07:55.477
Villanova's thermal lab is also on the NVIDIA-led Omnicool project inside ARPAE's cooler chips program.

00:07:56.097 --> 00:08:00.117
Google, Microsoft, and Meta are among the industry partners behind the center.

00:08:00.117 --> 00:08:05.297
The number to walk is the center's target, not a saving this donation has posted.

00:08:05.977 --> 00:08:10.817
ES2 wants U.S. data center energy efficiency up by 20-35%.

00:08:11.087 --> 00:08:16.377
By the center's own estimate, that band equals removing 1-2 power plants every 3 years,

00:08:16.977 --> 00:08:19.057
read it as a goal tied to a percent range.

00:08:19.697 --> 00:08:23.897
The IR-150 is the instrument for studying that range at rack scale.

00:08:24.357 --> 00:08:26.037
Not the proof the range has been hit.

00:08:26.037 --> 00:08:31.697
Richard Bonner, Excelsius' chief technology officer, cast the gift as joint research

00:08:31.697 --> 00:08:33.977
with the company's building AI infrastructure.

00:08:34.677 --> 00:08:40.117
Alfonso Ortega, the ES2 site director at Villanova, said researchers get a rack-level

00:08:40.117 --> 00:08:43.357
look at two-phase direct-to-chip as thermal-demand rises.

00:08:44.057 --> 00:08:50.097
The article's install line, early October 2026, falls before the November 3rd announcement,

00:08:50.417 --> 00:08:53.837
so the partnership and the hardware class are the facts you can use.

00:08:53.837 --> 00:08:58.897
That integrated two-phase rack stops being the right install when the hall can hold junction

00:08:58.897 --> 00:09:02.217
temperature with the air or single-phase loop it already has.

00:09:02.737 --> 00:09:09.437
The IR-150 exists so a lab can treat the rack, boiling plate and CDU together, as the

00:09:09.437 --> 00:09:10.217
thermal object.

00:09:10.737 --> 00:09:16.977
If the cabinet never reaches the load behind that 20-35% problem, the frame is a research tool

00:09:16.977 --> 00:09:19.237
in a room that did not need a phase change.

